  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "src/ui/cockpit/styles/shell.css",
      "content": "The shell styles only wrap the tabs; nothing lays out `.cockpit-rail` beside `.cockpit-drawers`. Both are block-level siblings in `.trade-detail`, and neither the existing styles nor the imported lane styles establish a two-column layout, so even on desktop the entire rail stacks above the drawers. Add a responsive shell layout that places the rail beside the drawers at wider widths (and keeps the integrity/incoherent banner spanning both columns), while stacking on narrow screens.",
      "existing_code": ".cockpit-drawers .tabs {\n  flex-wrap: wrap;\n}",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 4,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/trade-detail/Cockpit.tsx",
      "content": "Changing drawers immediately unmounts JournalDrawer, including any open DebtForm. That form stores answers/reason in local state and clears onDirtyChange on unmount, so clicking another tab (or using arrow-key activation) silently discards an unsaved reflection. Preserve the draft outside the mounted panel, or guard both click and keyboard drawer changes with an explicit discard confirmation. Add a regression case that edits a reflection, changes drawers, and returns to Journal.",
      "existing_code": "              onClick={() =\u003e setSelected(name)}",
      "start_line": 130,
      "end_line": 130,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/trade-detail/Cockpit.tsx",
      "content": "Make the panel keyboard-focusable with tabIndex={0}. Plan and Risk contains only static content, and Price History currently renders nothing, so pressing Tab from those selected tabs skips the panel entirely. A focusable panel is needed for the WAI-ARIA tabs pattern when its first content is not focusable.",
      "suggestion_code": "        \u003cdiv role=\"tabpanel\" id={`drawer-panel-${tabId(current)}`} aria-labelledby={`drawer-tab-${tabId(current)}`} tabIndex={0}\u003e",
      "existing_code": "        \u003cdiv role=\"tabpanel\" id={`drawer-panel-${tabId(current)}`} aria-labelledby={`drawer-tab-${tabId(current)}`}\u003e",
      "start_line": 136,
      "end_line": 136,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/trade-detail/Cockpit.tsx",
      "content": "Resolved reflections also regress after a drawer round trip: OwedDebtItem keeps its saved result only in local `settled` state, while TradeDetail never refreshes `view.journal` after the save. Unmounting this drawer drops that result; returning renders the original debt as 'Reflection owed' with Reflect now controls even though it was already resolved. Persist the saved outcome above the panel or update/refetch the journal after resolution, and cover save → another drawer → Journal.",
      "existing_code": "          \u003cJournalDrawer facade={facade} {...shell} {...(onDirtyChange \u0026\u0026 { onDirtyChange })} /\u003e",
      "start_line": 98,
      "end_line": 98,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/trade-detail/Cockpit.tsx",
      "content": "The rail and drawers still render as vertically stacked blocks, rather than the required side-by-side cockpit on wide screens. Neither `cockpit-rail`, `cockpit-drawers`, nor their `trade-detail` parent has a grid/flex layout rule (the only new shell rule wraps the tabs). Add a responsive layout for these siblings, keeping the integrity banner full-width and collapsing to one column on narrow screens.",
      "existing_code": "      \u003cdiv className=\"cockpit-drawers\"\u003e",
      "start_line": 118,
      "end_line": 118,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
